cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use SpectroElectroChem Suite in scientific work, please cite the software using the metadata below."
title: "SpectroElectroChem Suite"
type: software
version: "5.5.1"
date-released: 2026-07-30
authors:
  - family-names: Habekost
    given-names: Achim
    email: A.Habekost@t-online.de
repository-code: "https://github.com/Achim-Habekost/SpectroElectroChem-Suite"
url: "https://github.com/Achim-Habekost/SpectroElectroChem-Suite"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - spectroelectrochemistry
  - electrochemistry
  - Raman spectroscopy
  - SERS
  - absorptovoltammetry
  - fluorovoltammetry
  - rotating ring-disk electrode
  - RRDE
  - Levich analysis
  - Koutecky-Levich analysis
  - Tafel analysis
  - Butler-Volmer kinetics
abstract: >-
  SpectroElectroChem Suite is an open-source Python application for the
  analysis, visualization and quantitative evaluation of spectroelectrochemical
  and rotating ring-disk electrode data. It provides graphical workflows for
  Raman spectra, Raman and SERS voltammograms, absorption and fluorescence
  voltammograms, and RRDE measurements, including publication-ready numerical
  and graphical exports.
